---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const BASE = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Felix Geelhaar — writes on operations, product, engineering, and team collaboration. Builds small tools, mostly Go."
  lede="The long version."
  nav="about"
  ogImage="about"
>
  <section class="prose">
    <p>
      I write about the operating models, product trade-offs, and engineering practices that
      decide whether teams ship clearly. The interesting layer for me is the connective
      tissue &mdash; how decisions move, where ownership lives, what a working agreement
      actually does. Less framework, more field notes.
    </p>
    <p>
      In parallel I build things. A handful of small tools, mostly Go, on
      <a href="https://github.com/felixgeelhaar">github.com/felixgeelhaar</a> &mdash;
      see <a href={`${BASE}lab`}>/lab</a> for the current shortlist.
    </p>
    <p>
      Background: 15+ years across engineering, platform, and ops roles &mdash; a mix of
      startups, scale-ups, and enterprise. Picked up JavaScript and PHP early, drifted into
      TypeScript, settled on Go for most things I ship today. I live near Munich. Currently
      focused on what's on <a href={`${BASE}now`}>/now</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Find me elsewhere</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/felixgeelhaar">GitHub</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/felixgeelhaar/">LinkedIn</a></li>
      <li><a href={`${BASE}contact`}>Email</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
